    <h1>Immigration Motions, Blacklist &amp; Derogatory Record Assistance</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Been told you're barred from re-entering the Philippines, or found a derogatory record attached to your name?</p>

    <p>Depending on the applicable immigration record, order or proceeding, our team can assist in identifying the appropriate procedural route and documentary requirements.</p>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Reviewing the immigration record, order or proceeding that applies to you</li>
      <li>Identifying the procedural options and documentary requirements available</li>
      <li>Preparing and lodging the appropriate motion or request, where applicable</li>
      <li>Keeping you informed throughout the process</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Matters We Assist With</h2>
    <p>Possible matters may include, where applicable:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Motions for Reconsideration</li>
      <li>Blacklist lifting</li>
      <li>Watchlist or other derogatory-record matters</li>
      <li>Verification of immigration records</li>
      <li>Requests for lifting or reconsideration</li>
      <li>Related immigration proceedings</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="context-note">
      <p>The appropriate procedural option depends on the nature of the immigration record, order or proceeding and the remedies available in the particular circumstances. Following an initial review, we can identify the relevant procedural options and documentary requirements.</p>
